# spec 046 Q77/Q82 — rebuildable caches, per-machine
market-data/
raw-data/
# evidence quote snapshots inside each thesis ARE committed

# Raw Claude session archives — large (~178 MB for 002; ~160 MB for 003's
# report window), kept on disk for provenance only. The human-readable record is
# session-history-*.md at the repo root; these are the primary source beneath it,
# not version-controlled.
#
# The trailing `*` covers every variant of the directory name — `session-history/`
# and `session-history-report/` today, anything else later. A bare
# `theses/*/session-history/` does NOT match `session-history-report/`, which
# would have left ~160 MB of raw context committable; verified with
# `git check-ignore` both ways before and after.
theses/*/session-history*/

# Per-machine cruft — never has content anyone wants, and both were already
# tracked before this rule existed (`theses/001-.../artifacts/.DS_Store`,
# `tools/__pycache__/plan_audit.cpython-311.pyc`). A .gitignore rule does NOT
# untrack an already-tracked path, so those two are removed from the index in the
# same commit; without that the rule would be cosmetic and the files would keep
# reappearing as modifications.
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
